vcctrl local patch 0002: resume an interrupted PS/2 mouse packet

Against 0001 (mouse delivery counters), which is against dekuNukem/USB4VC
firmware/ibmpc at ae3813d. Reports as firmware 0.5.108.

Stock firmware abandons a mouse packet on a mid-byte host inhibit, or on a
bus held more than 200 ms between bytes. If a byte had already gone out, the
host holds part of a packet. CuteMouse 2.1b4 keeps those bytes, so every
later packet is read shifted for as long as the driver runs. Measured
2026-11-11 on the Gateway 2000 (dosags round RJ, cells RJM1 and RJM2): every
click after the first pkt_partial landed at the bottom-left of the screen
until the cell ended (vcctrl docs/MOUSE.md sec. 10).

This patch:
  - keeps the built packet, and the index of the next byte, until the host
    has all of it. A mid-byte inhibit resends that same byte (the host
    discards an incomplete one). A bus that is not idle is waited out, and
    then only the REMAINING bytes are sent.
  - waits without blocking: each pass tries for 2 ms, then returns to the
    main loop, so the keyboard is still serviced. Stock blocked both for up
    to 200 ms per byte.
  - still gives a packet up in two cases, counted as a loss on the layout-1
    page exactly as before: when the host sends a command (a PS/2 device
    drops its output then), or when the wait budget runs out (1 s if no byte
    went out, 5 s once one had).
  - stops consolidating at a button change, so a press and its release are
    never OR-ed into a hold. edge_merged therefore stays 0. Movement is
    summed and capped at +-127 exactly as before, so a move over 127 is
    still clipped. Callers calibrated against that are unaffected.
  - adds a second counter page. MOSI 0x41 -> MISO 0xC1, layout 1:
      bytes 0-3: 0xCD, seq echo, 0xC1, layout
      bytes 4-15: 6 x uint16 LE: pkt_resumed, inhibit_retry, partial_waits,
                  superseded, abandon_budget, max_wait_ms
    The 0x40 page is unchanged in layout AND meaning (pkt_* loss counters
    still mean "never fully delivered"). A Pi that only knows 0x40 keeps
    working.

Not done here: 0xFE (resend) still only ACKs; host_fe has never moved on this
rig. ps2kb.c is untouched.

